  "Id": 3474,
  "Title": "CIME & SPIE Partnered with TDF MagnifiScience Centre for \"Rescue Rangers\" Workshop",
  "NewsSubTitle": null,
  "NewsSummary": "Aga Khan University CIME partnered with TDF MagnifiScience Centre to host an innovative workshop known as \"Rescue Rangers: Junior Doctor Adventure.\" ",
  "GlobalNews": false,
  "AlternateNewsTitle": null,
  "AlternateNewsSubtitle": null,
  "AlternateNewsSummary": null,
  "NewsContent": "<div class=\"ExternalClassFC60329094DE47A1B675D241A95F9EB1\"><p><br></p><p>CIME partnered with TDF MagnifiScience Centre to host an innovative workshop known as &quot;Rescue Rangers&#58; Junior Doctor Adventure.&quot; The goal of this unique event was to be both educational and exciting, providing an opportunity for participants to develop crucial first aid skills and critical thinking abilities.</p><p>The event was a collaborative effort between SPIE, the student-led simulation society, and the CIME team. They conducted three engaging sessions at the TDF Museum, where participants enjoyed a hands-on, holistic learning experience. Every session of the workshop featured four interactive stations&#58;</p><p>Electrocution Station&#58; Participants learned how to handle electric currents and shocks safely.</p><p>CPR Station&#58; Children were taught basic CPR skills with the guidance of a CPR professional.</p><p>Burn Station&#58; Participants learned how to manage burns effectively.</p><p>Bleeding Station&#58; Children were taught techniques to stop bleeding instantly.</p><p>The workshop served as a qualitative research tool for the education team at CIME to study parental perceptions of community-based simulations for teaching children life-saving skills. The workshop successfully combined education with excitement, leaving a lasting impact on the participants.<br></p></div>",
